{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 16{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=16{x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 16{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=4{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 16{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(x)(4{x}^{4})-\\int \\frac{4{x}^{4}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5"} {"question" "q-78961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(1-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{4{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-2x+C \\\\  & =2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C"] ["math" "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] ["math" "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] ["math" "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)+1)+C"] ["math" "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x-3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-\\int \\frac{x}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $x-3=u,$ thus $x=u+3$ and $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-\\int \\frac{x}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-\\int \\frac{u+3}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-\\int \\,\\text{d}u-3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u} \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-u-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡u+D \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-(x-3)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)+D \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-x+3+D \\\\  & =(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D+3$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)+C"] ["math" "(2x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-x+C"] ["math" "(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)+3x+C"] ["math" "(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-6x+C"] ["math" "(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-114592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-3)-x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-351016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-351016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}-{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,(x){|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}-{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}x(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{log}_{3}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3}}{8})\\,(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8})-{log}_{3}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{1}{8})\\,(\\frac{1}{8})]-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}{log}_{3}⁡({e}^{3})-\\frac{1}{8}{log}_{3}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}x{|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(2{e}^{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-351016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5"} {"question" "q-351016" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"} {"question" "q-351016" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2e^3+1}{8\\ln(3)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5353f6d29bba149cbb3a8804a61ee64152bbeaf387703e896f4f365475c590d"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1230 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
